<style id="shila-responsive-images">
/* ============================================================
   v18 ROOT-CAUSE FIX — Problem A
   Browser inspection (puppeteer @1280w) measured the
   .embed-responsive.embed-responsive-1by1 wrapper around
   shila-5.webp:
     - element padding-bottom = 273.7px  (from v17 rule)
     - ::before  padding-top  = 273.7px  (from v17 rule)
     - resulting offsetHeight = 547.4px (487 wide) — that's 1:1.125
   Both rules STACKED instead of one overriding the other,
   doubling the reserved aspect. The image (16:9) was then
   object-fit:contain'd into a near-1:1 box -> ~137px of empty
   whitespace ABOVE and BELOW the image. That is the "HUGE empty
   white box above the doctor+anatomy image" the user reported.

   Fix: blow away padding-bottom on the element AND the ::before
   pseudo-element, then use modern aspect-ratio with !important.
   This wins over both Bootstrap's stock .embed-responsive-1by1::before
   { padding-top:100% } AND any stale v17 padding-bottom in cache.
   ============================================================ */
.embed-responsive.embed-responsive-1by1{
  /* Reset the doubled padding from v17 */
  padding-bottom:0 !important;
  padding-top:0 !important;
  position:relative !important;
  overflow:hidden !important;
  /* Use modern aspect-ratio. Image is 1138x640 = 16:9. */
  aspect-ratio:16 / 9 !important;
  height:auto !important;
}
.embed-responsive.embed-responsive-1by1::before{
  /* Bootstrap defaults to padding-top:100%; we kill it entirely
     because aspect-ratio on the parent now governs height. */
  content:none !important;
  display:none !important;
  padding-top:0 !important;
  padding-bottom:0 !important;
  height:0 !important;
}
.embed-responsive.embed-responsive-1by1 .embed-responsive-item,
.embed-responsive.embed-responsive-1by1 img{
  position:absolute !important;
  top:0 !important;
  left:0 !important;
  width:100% !important;
